THIRD-PARTY NOTICES
===================

Asterisco is MIT-licensed (see LICENSE). It bundles third-party
open-source components, each under its own license. All current dependencies
are under permissive licenses (MIT / Apache-2.0 / ISC / BSD / Unicode /
MPL-2.0). Copyleft (GPL/AGPL/LGPL) dependencies are excluded — accepting one
would force the whole project to relicense — so verify any new dependency's
license before adding it.

Regenerate the notices
-----------------------

    bun run notices

This runs `cargo about` over the Rust crates and `generate-license-file` over
the npm tree, then concatenates both into the file that actually ships with
the app:

    src-tauri/THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt

That file is committed and bundled as a packaging resource (see
`tauri.conf.json`'s `bundle.resources` and `docs/RELEASING.md`); it is what
users see from Settings → "View third-party notices". This root-level file is
a short pointer to it, not a copy.
